> T Muramasa &

A powerfull weapon for when it arrives in the game but better
artifacts catch up later in the game.  It's two-handed and
current versions of Nethack make that a nearly fatal
disadvantage in the late stages of the game.

> Snickersnee
> I just sacraficed and got Snickersnee.  Seems like a waste to me.

Why a waste?  Among non-artifact weapons katana is one
of the best.  They give better damage than the more common
long sword and they are in the same skills class as the
long sword.  Folks who go without artifacts tend to be
carrying long swords or katanas when they ascend.  And
Snickersnee is better than any other katana.

> If I use Tsurugi of Muramasa I cannot #twoweapon
> What should I use?

For what you have, Snickersnee beats the rest.  Build your
long sword skill towards Expert then switch to #twoweapon
with some nice non-artifact weapon and build the #twoweapon
skill.

But you have an assortment of other artifact weapons
available to use.  As lawfull you have two surefire ways of
getting Excalibur and for an assortment of reasons it beats
even Snickersnee.  There are two artifact weapons that any
character can have but neither is as good as Snickersnee
at this point.

And you can continue to #offer without #pray'ing and you'll
eventually get artifacts better than either Snickersnee or
Excalibur.  Greyswandir, Frost Brand and depending on
personal tastes Fire Brand.



